# For a host (`deno task host`): Caddy in front provides HTTPS for the host's main name and for every
# name under it, getting a certificate for each name the first time someone asks for it. Before it
# does, it asks the host program whether the name is one of its own, so nobody can make it fetch
# certificates for names that lead nowhere. Install Caddy with the system's package manager, put this
# in /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and reload Caddy. See host/README.md.

{
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://127.0.0.1:8000/endlessmind/known
	}
}

https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
